# Python skill routing

When working on Python files, load the matching skill from `.cursor/skills/` or
`~/.cursor/skills/` before starting:

| Task | Skill |
|------|-------|
| Writing or changing code | `python-development` |
| Tests, TDD, coverage | `python-testing` |
| Failures and wrong behavior | `python-debugging` |
| Review of a diff or file | `python-code-review` |
| Restructuring without behavior change | `python-refactoring` |
| Dependencies, pyproject.toml, builds | `python-packaging` |
| Speed and memory | `python-performance` |
| Untrusted input, secrets, auth | `python-security` |
| Docstrings, README, API docs | `python-documentation` |
| pandas, Polars, ETL | `python-data-engineering` |

Technology skills apply only when the technology is a project dependency:
`fastapi`, `django`, `sqlalchemy`, `postgresql`, `docker`, `ci-cd`,
`machine-learning`, `observability`.
